WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.265
- Bon appetit! (laughs)

00:00:01.265 --> 00:00:02.606
- What's gonna happen?

00:00:02.606 --> 00:00:05.273
(playful music)

00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:08.336
- In France we have, our French
fries are a little bigger,

00:00:08.336 --> 00:00:09.641
a little thicker.

00:00:09.641 --> 00:00:12.891
- I have had McDonald's
French fries in France,

00:00:12.891 --> 00:00:16.137
and in Luxembourg, and in
the UK, but never in the US.

00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:18.334
- And McDonalds adapts
the taste per country

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:19.799
for the country culture,

00:00:19.799 --> 00:00:21.595
so each country is different tastes.

00:00:21.595 --> 00:00:25.418
- So far my favorite McDonalds
food is by far in France,

00:00:25.418 --> 00:00:28.145
because the meat is better,
the sauces are nicer,

00:00:28.145 --> 00:00:33.049
so we're looking forward to
see how different it is here.

00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:35.982
- They smell, they smell fresh and fatty,

00:00:35.982 --> 00:00:37.618
we can smell the oil, definitely.

00:00:37.618 --> 00:00:38.451
- Yeah.

00:00:38.451 --> 00:00:41.445
- They're very light,
a bit mushy. (laughs)

00:00:41.445 --> 00:00:42.710
That's point.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.354
- Tastes like potatoes, tastes
like what it should taste.

00:00:45.354 --> 00:00:48.771
- It tastes more plasticky, right?

00:00:48.771 --> 00:00:50.222
Like it's been sitting there for awhile.

00:00:50.222 --> 00:00:52.555
- I think the smell is
the best thing, honestly,

00:00:52.555 --> 00:00:53.900
when you first get your Big Mac--

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.939
- Can you smell anything else than salt?

00:00:55.939 --> 00:00:56.772
(laughs)

00:00:56.772 --> 00:00:59.522
- These are not traditional French fries.

00:00:59.522 --> 00:01:02.119
They are a bit more crispy,
a bit more salty, but,

00:01:02.119 --> 00:01:03.419
they taste fine with me.

00:01:03.419 --> 00:01:04.475
- It lacks salt.

00:01:04.475 --> 00:01:05.572
- And it's not crispy enough.

00:01:05.572 --> 00:01:07.700
- Doesn't taste as much,
not crispy enough, too oily.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.775
- I can see it in my hands.

00:01:08.775 --> 00:01:12.647
- I can see it, yeah,
it's still on my hand too.

00:01:12.647 --> 00:01:14.922
- [Both] We prefer French fries from home.

00:01:14.922 --> 00:01:17.825
- French fries in France are legit,

00:01:17.825 --> 00:01:21.560
they're the real thing, you
know, it was a whole potato.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:24.855
- I thought the fries are
fine, just, greasy and small,

00:01:24.855 --> 00:01:26.073
like they've always been.

00:01:26.073 --> 00:01:28.761
- Our French fries are a little
bigger, a little thicker,

00:01:28.761 --> 00:01:30.186
but I like this one, they are like,

00:01:30.186 --> 00:01:31.643
actually a little easier to eat.

00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:33.759
- It didn't seem as fresh
here, didn't seem as--

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.109
- Not fresh, too oily.

00:01:35.109 --> 00:01:36.978
The freshness is a very important thing,

00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:40.594
to eat fast food you want it
to be very fresh, very tasty,

00:01:40.594 --> 00:01:42.872
and if it's not, your disappointed.

00:01:42.872 --> 00:01:45.313
- I like them, I can't
say I'd go and eat them

00:01:45.313 --> 00:01:47.808
all the time but, they're
a little guilty pleasure

00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:48.997
when I do.

00:01:48.997 --> 00:01:52.247
(soft xylophone music)

00:01:55.049 --> 00:01:56.377
(sign creaks)

